comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-19T09:33:02.490Z",codex,"Duplicate check: complete strict186-item all-status corpus, request-specific search and open/in-progress inventories inspected suffix-date owner pmc-lnyt, shipped prepublish isolation pmc-xioo and historical manual readiness owners pmc-qjl9 and pmc-nv97. Historical manual suffix cuts used --tag latest successfully, but no current workflow owner covers its omitted dist-tag. Source evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/39228085609 ."
  "2026-10-19T09:36:27.061Z",codex,"Real offline npm keeper fails before the single-argument correction with the same mandatory-dist-tag refusal as hosted npm11.19.0. It extracts the executed publisher's literal argv and adds only dry-run/offline controls in a synthetic package with isolated empty configs/cache and a non-routable registry; no real publication or credentials. Add explicit --tag latest while retaining --access public, provenance and ignore-scripts. Document that stable caret ranges intentionally await the next dated stable release, whereas latest/exact consumers receive the manual suffix cut."
  "2026-10-19T09:38:54.843Z",codex,"The real npm acceptance now passes after adding only --tag latest:19/19 workflow/date/publish tests, zero skips/failures, plus linked execution, typecheck,169-declaration docstring gate and canonical provenance auditor. The initial deterministic npm11.19 refusal and10-minute reconciliation failure are retained. Same-day counter SemVer behavior is documented explicitly; retry the existing untagged2026.10.19-1 only after reviewed merge."
  "2026-10-19T09:43:34.376Z",codex,"Ownership hygiene: live full reads identify pmc-38z4, pmc-rspo and pmc-ctr2 as explicitly released historical verifier handoffs; return them to open instead of leaving unclaimed work in progress. Existing pmc-6edv and pmc-wgte carry other-principal ownership and are not overridden. Only this publisher fix and the actively verified suffix handoff were claimed in this delivery; both are released after evidence closure."
